{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/984849-supplements-to-adventure","id":984849,"title":"Supplements to Adventure!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Adventure!"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-10T06:29:40-07:00","id":984849,"title":"Supplements to Adventure!","content":"I know I'm way ahead of the schedule, but assuming <i><b>Adventure!</b></i> get the attention it deserves which supplements would you like to see?<br /> <br /> Are there any pulp genres that you would look forward to more than others? Are there any parts of the old book that were more interesting than the others?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3307-ifrippe","name":"ifrippe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T07:36:07-07:00","id":984869,"title":"","content":"something i would wish for adventure! would be a supplement about weird and strange places.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/24.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/619-deadguy","name":"DeadGuy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T11:12:20-07:00","id":984959,"title":"","content":"I'd love to see a splat on vehicles and tech for the era. Zeppelins and steampunk vehicles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=485\" data-tempid=\"temp_485_1538393298974_786\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1277-karpomatic","name":"karpomatic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1277_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T15:23:09-07:00","id":985101,"title":"","content":"A book that describes the organizations would be fantastic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T20:44:54-07:00","id":985251,"title":"","content":"I think I'd like a WW2 supplement. I know it's not a war game but could introduce some interesting save the world from mad scientists etc elements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7165-queen-anne-country","name":"Queen Anne Country","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T13:08:52-07:00","id":985621,"title":"","content":"Giving Adventure! a greater lease on life would be an amazing thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T05:25:57-07:00","id":988210,"title":"","content":"About antagonist with vampire powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T12:34:47-07:00","id":988979,"title":"","content":"I'd really like to see some location specific work for Adventure! I'm thinking something like Adventure! Australia or Adventure! Africa. Of course, with the time frame setting of Adventure! there will be some tropes involved in these books, but I think you can juxtapose the worldview of the Aeon Society by having these books look at that impact of the Hammersmith Incident on these places. What would be interesting is to create a series of stories that drive characters around the world to figure out how the Hammersmith Incident has caused that dispersal of Z waves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Find my products on the ST Vault here: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/225678/Dark-New-England-Five-Chronicle-Jumpstarts-Bundle?affiliate_id=235787\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.storytellersvault.com/pro...iate_id=235787</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12515-inclusivegaming","name":"InclusiveGaming","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T14:25:07-07:00","id":991113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Queen Anne Country</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/984849-supplements-to-adventure?p=985251#post985251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I'd like a WW2 supplement. I know it's not a war game but could introduce some interesting save the world from mad scientists etc elements.</div> </div> </div> </div>You really haven't done superhero/adventure properly until you've fought a Giant Nazi Robot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T15:45:23-07:00","id":991152,"title":"","content":"WWII is twenty years outside the Adventure! timeframe. That's not an Adventure! supplement, that's a different era entirely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T17:28:35-07:00","id":991189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/984849-supplements-to-adventure?p=991152#post991152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WWII is twenty years outside the Adventure! timeframe. That's not an Adventure! supplement, that's a different era entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div>IanWatson: #PartyPooper OR #HintDropper ?? <br /> <br /> I think I may've been thinking about the disappearance of Primoris in '43.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7165-queen-anne-country","name":"Queen Anne Country","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T10:15:49-07:00","id":992448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/984849-supplements-to-adventure?p=991152#post991152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WWII is twenty years outside the Adventure! timeframe. That's not an Adventure! supplement, that's a different era entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div>So...does that mean you're considering a game in that era? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T21:39:41-07:00","id":992760,"title":"","content":"Not at this time, I'm not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T05:28:09-07:00","id":992894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/984849-supplements-to-adventure?p=992760#post992760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not at this time, I'm not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> well, it's ok plenty of cool stuff already on line. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T23:09:15-08:00","id":1002134,"title":"","content":"The Zeppelins sourcebook is a must. I'd also like to see sourcebooks for Space Opera and Planetary Romance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T05:16:21-08:00","id":1005669,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">WW 2 might be outside the time fram but Hitler and the Nazi Party were active by 1924 so that is a possibility.<br /> <br /> I like to see and expansion of Daredevil abilities and Weird Science</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6379-tytalan","name":"tytalan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T06:54:07-08:00","id":1016522,"title":"","content":"I'd love to see Adventure! roll with it's self-awareness and have supplements for archvillains, sidekicks, twist endings and other literary tropes. Like Astromancer suggests, i could be entertained by a set on different genres of stories, romance, mystery, horror, sci-fi, etc...<br /> The original Adventure! was a kind of light hearted and youthful setting, the wonders and terrors of telluric strangeness were brank-spanking new, entirely emergent and fresh. I agree that in many ways WWII just doesn't fit the setting's mood - the meta-plot has this sad meltdown of the friendship between Mercer and Donighal about that time so really signify how much things have changed by then. It feels like leaving the silver age of comics at that point, i think. WWII is industrial war and inspiration may have been affected by that shift in the global zietgiest.<br /> <br /> As for vehicles and technology, i'd really prefer that they it all get rolled into the same system - so that converting an Adventure! era submarine or machine gun to Aberrant or even Trinity rules wouldn't require intense cross-referencing against other weapons from the destination game. But, i've heard this is planned anyway - so, yeah, a single book/title to cover all the wierd and wonderful shapes that vehicles (and machine consciousness) can take would be great, kind of like GURPS did.<br /> <br /> Tytalan also has good suggestions, the Invention system always deserved it's own book, also preferably not tied to any single setting. Daredevils received the least attention of any in the original print run, but from what i recall the first published book OP is doing is a kind of starter book with only Daredevils for now (but, it's been a while, i could be wrong about that).<br /> <br /> Inclusive Gaming mentions a series of releases on various world locations, and while that could be a minefield to write - it would suite the setting at least. Hopefully the readers would understand that it's meant to reflect the period and not the viewpoints of the authors, because to properly capture the feeling of old pulp novels there is might be a fair amount of casual racism/sexism. Max makes it pretty clear he doesn't tolerate that in his society for <i>gentlemen</i>, but it's a prickly subject either way.<br /> -shrug-","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T13:50:57-08:00","id":1017295,"title":"","content":"I think you mean the Golden Age of comics; the Silver Age didn't start until 1956. In my game, the Adventure! era ran from the Hammersmith experiment through the end of WWII, with things getting progressively more noir-ish as time went on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T14:58:41-08:00","id":1017337,"title":"","content":"One more thing: in my timeline, both Adventure! and Aberrant end tragically, Adventure! with the final battle between Aeon and Primoris, Aberrant with the Aberrant War. Only Aeon ends on a hopeful note.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T23:55:27-08:00","id":1017520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/984849-supplements-to-adventure?p=1016522#post1016522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Daredevils received the least attention of any in the original print run, but from what i recall the first published book OP is doing is a kind of starter book with only Daredevils for now (but, it's been a while, i could be wrong about that).</div> </div> </div> </div>The Trinity Continuum corebook will have a modern-day setting, with rules for baseline humans and Talents (the modern-day name for daredevils).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T04:22:25-08:00","id":1017584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JulianMoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/984849-supplements-to-adventure?p=1017295#post1017295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you mean the Golden Age of comics; the Silver Age didn't start until 1956. In my game, the Adventure! era ran from the Hammersmith experiment through the end of WWII, with things getting progressively more noir-ish as time went on.</div> </div> </div> </div>,.-:-.,<br /> Of course, thanks for pointing it out. But, i'm speaking more about the mood then the time-periods, Golden and even some platinum age sources (Safari Jack, Scalper Dutch) make for the start of the Hammersmith era, but an important marker seperating the gold from the silver to me is that the silver age begins and continues to focus on teams - the Justice League, the Fantastic Four and more common cameo's from other titles. That's the silver age stuff i meant - i'm looking forward to seeing what OPP do with the fifties, but i always assumed the great tragedy of the hammersmith era was that it faded away into the mundane and by the cold war fifties mostly only a few unconsciouly special talents remained (James Bond, John Rambo, etc...) - the telluric locales vanished with everything inside them as if they had never existed. But i agree that the great tragedy of Aberrant was the war even though at times it's hard to reconcile that against some of the forces and at play that were probably available to the planet between 2049 and 2061.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/984849-supplements-to-adventure?p=1017520#post1017520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Trinity Continuum corebook will have a modern-day setting, with rules for baseline humans and Talents (the modern-day name for daredevils).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ,.-:-.,<br /> Thanks for that, i thought it would be a bit less than modern for some reason, but like i said, it's been a while.<br /> Apologies for the tangent, just in the mood to reply, despite having little else to add to the topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4458,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","user":"Nihilist","date":".  Tangent embraced 12-15-2016, 07:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T18:10:01-08:00","id":1017883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/984849-supplements-to-adventure?p=1002134#post1002134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Zeppelins sourcebook is a must. I'd also like to see sourcebooks for Space Opera and Planetary Romance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm torn between wanting this set specifically in the Adventure! Era, and having parallel timeline that stays pulpy so you get the Planetary Romance version of the 22nd Century with Mesmerists running around like Jedi.<br /> <br /> Of course, if the pulpy locals of Adventure! do fade away in the official timeline, they could just have continued as their own parallel timeline and be viable as such anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T13:23:13-08:00","id":1018204,"title":"","content":"I like to imagine that each of the three games is its own timeline, with echoes of important people and events in the other two timelines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T22:38:33-08:00","id":1018350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/984849-supplements-to-adventure?p=1018204#post1018204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like to imagine that each of the three games is its own timeline, with echoes of important people and events in the other two timelines.</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC, what Ian's said is that each game has their past fixed but their future open-ended. So for example the TC corebook assumes Adventure! happened, but not that Aberrant or Aeon will happen.<br /> <br /> And, well, Ian <i>has</i> said the Continuum's a multiverse...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":51,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","user":"marin","date":". 12-17-2016, 06:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T02:32:14-08:00","id":1018386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/984849-supplements-to-adventure?p=1017883#post1017883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm torn between wanting this set specifically in the Adventure! Era, and having parallel timeline that stays pulpy so you get the Planetary Romance version of the 22nd Century with Mesmerists running around like Jedi.<br /> <br /> Of course, if the pulpy locals of Adventure! do fade away in the official timeline, they could just have continued as their own parallel timeline and be viable as such anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why not both? Personally, i have always played the weird-fantastic places as &quot;Schrodinger locales&quot; existing both <i>in</i> and <i>outside</i> our continuum, sometimes both, depending on circunstances and i guess the same conceit could be applied here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T03:31:57-08:00","id":1018400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/984849-supplements-to-adventure?p=1018350#post1018350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> IIRC, what Ian's said is that each game has their past fixed but their future open-ended. So for example the TC corebook assumes Adventure! happened, but not that Aberrant or Aeon will happen.<br /> <br /> And, well, Ian <i>has</i> said the Continuum's a multiverse...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I've seen those comments, and I was basically agreeing with them.<br /> <br /> I first started looking at it this way back in 1999 or so, but there were a lot of issues with Adventure -&gt; Aberrant -&gt; Trinity that could only really be resolved with a multiverse rather than a single universe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T05:23:10-08:00","id":1018426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/984849-supplements-to-adventure?p=1018400#post1018400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I first started looking at it this way back in 1999 or so, but there were a lot of issues with Adventure -&gt; Aberrant -&gt; Trinity that could only really be resolved with a multiverse rather than a single universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you ever see the (unofficial) Trinity Storyteller's Handbook explanation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T05:42:38-08:00","id":1018432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/984849-supplements-to-adventure?p=1018426#post1018426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did you ever see the (unofficial) Trinity Storyteller's Handbook explanation?</div> </div> </div> </div>I probably did but I don't recall it. What is it? Is it the one about Mercer splitting into different timelines?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T06:35:22-08:00","id":1018438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/984849-supplements-to-adventure?p=1018432#post1018432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I probably did but I don't recall it. What is it? Is it the one about Mercer splitting into different timelines?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that one (<a href=\"http://rpgbooks.wikia.com/wiki/Trinity_Storytellers_Handbook/Chapter_One:_The_%C3%86on_Trinity\" target=\"_blank\">the writeup's available at the end of this page</a>).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T13:14:46-08:00","id":1018561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/984849-supplements-to-adventure?p=1018438#post1018438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, that one (<a href=\"http://rpgbooks.wikia.com/wiki/Trinity_Storytellers_Handbook/Chapter_One:_The_%C3%86on_Trinity\" target=\"_blank\">the writeup's available at the end of this page</a>).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah yeah, that one was floating around a bit at the time and I definitely like it as an explanation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T15:54:59-08:00","id":1041537,"title":"","content":"If one is to dream ...<br /> <br /> Period pulp horror in the view of Lovecraft, Howard, Hodgson, Blackwood, and the like, incorporating the ideas of forbidden knowledge, alien/non-human influences, and disturbing scientific theories into Adventure!<br /> <br /> Western pulp. <br /> <br /> And a collection of places along the lines of the Hollow Earth, Atlantis, Shambhala, Thule, Mars, and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T15:54:28-08:00","id":1043758,"title":"","content":"As much as I would like to see a world war two sourcebook, the more I thought about it the more I realized Adventure! wouldn't fit. The pulp style and ideals cannot survive so much horror. A different game with a different tone is needed.<br /> <br /> Back to the question at hand, here's what I would love to see expanded from the main book.<br /> <br /> -Supplement dedicated to mad scientists, their inventions, crafting, and gadgets,<br /> -Supplement with extra information about stalwards, mesmerists, and daredevils, with extra knacks.<br /> -Suplement expanding information about the organizations and how to create your own. Possibly with new ones.<br /> -Supplement with information about ancient civilizations, conspiracies, world secrets and how to use them in your game.<br /> -Supplement exploring the future of the setting if the pulp ideals triumphed and managed to prevent the great depresion and the world war.<br /> <br /> And that's it for now. I'll add more If I can think of any.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T17:42:14-08:00","id":1043780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/984849-supplements-to-adventure?p=1043758#post1043758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Supplement dedicated to mad scientists, their inventions, crafting, and gadgets,</div> </div> </div> </div>This would, as they said back in the day, rock on toast.<br /> <br /> I sometimes imagine Adventure! being done the same way all of White Wolf's early WoD games were done, with splatbooks for Daredevils, Mesmerists, and Stalwarts, city/setting books (New York, Hollywood, Berlin), and so on. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T08:23:45-08:00","id":1045772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/984849-supplements-to-adventure?p=1041537#post1041537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Period pulp horror in the view of Lovecraft, Howard, Hodgson, Blackwood, and the like, incorporating the ideas of forbidden knowledge, alien/non-human influences, and disturbing scientific theories into Adventure!</div> </div> </div> </div>Overlapping with that, I'd like to see a book on occultism, &quot;magic,&quot; and psychic phenomena -- probably taking a pseudoscientific approach, as befits the Continuum. Fewer bells, books and candles; more ectoplasm and electric pentacles. That said, 1920s-era ideas about psychic powers are still pretty different from the later SF that inspired Aeon/Trinity, and I'd like to see a supplement reflecting that. Obviously, this could also double as a Mesmer book, although there's room for Daredevils and Stalwarts to get in on the fun, too. The idea of achieving superhuman mental and physical abilities through rigorous training was a staple of the pulps; just look at Doc Savage!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/40-dspaul","name":"DSPaul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T14:05:28-08:00","id":1181789,"title":"","content":"I wonder if they'll even use the title Aventure! In the new edition!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T15:25:12-08:00","id":1181821,"title":"","content":"I have always believed that the proper title is <b>TWO-FISTED TALES OF SHERE DAMN MANLY ADVENTURE!</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T15:44:43-08:00","id":1181829,"title":"","content":"While I'm thinking about it, it'd be kind of cool to have a sourcebook specifically about female characters. What life was like for women of different classes, races, countries, etc. in the 1920s, ways to get around various restrictions (including pointing out ones people may think exist because of &quot;common knowledge&quot; but actually don't), a look at female characters in the period Pulps (including how to invert and subvert various stereotypes and genre tropes), the close cousins to the Pulps including female detective stories, aviatrix fiction, radio dramas, newspaper comics, and so forth, maybe a discussion of lesbianism in the 1920s and 30s, things to think about when making female villains and other NPCs, ideas and examples of all-female organizations, and maybe include a dozen or so female NPCs that can serve as allies, mentors, rivals, enemies, plot hooks and what not. <br /> <br /> I'm probably one of the few people who'd buy such a book, sadly, but it'd be kind of cool to have it as maybe a special March release for National (American) Women's History Month and International Women's Day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T18:20:55-08:00","id":1181877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/984849-supplements-to-adventure?p=1181829#post1181829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I'm thinking about it, it'd be kind of cool to have a sourcebook specifically about female characters. What life was like for women of different classes, races, countries, etc. in the 1920s, ways to get around various restrictions (including pointing out ones people may think exist because of &amp;quot;common knowledge&amp;quot; but actually don't), a look at female characters in the period Pulps (including how to invert and subvert various stereotypes and genre tropes), the close cousins to the Pulps including female detective stories, aviatrix fiction, radio dramas, newspaper comics, and so forth, maybe a discussion of lesbianism in the 1920s and 30s, things to think about when making female villains and other NPCs, ideas and examples of all-female organizations, and maybe include a dozen or so female NPCs that can serve as allies, mentors, rivals, enemies, plot hooks and what not. <br /> <br /> I'm probably one of the few people who'd buy such a book, sadly, but it'd be kind of cool to have it as maybe a special March release for National (American) Women's History Month and International Women's Day.</div> </div> </div> </div>It sounds cool to me too. A book on including other groups left out of pulp adventure like non-whites (nicely attacked by the Mississippi Slim vignettes in the book) or the problems of a gay male couple in period.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T18:37:23-08:00","id":1181881,"title":"","content":"There was supposed to be a book on that very subject for a different game line (about 10 years ago IIRC), looking at everything from women, blacks and gays to even German and Japanese nationals in the 20s and 30s, but I've no idea if it ever actually came out or even which game line it was meant for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T00:30:53-08:00","id":1181933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/984849-supplements-to-adventure?p=1181877#post1181877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It sounds cool to me too. A book on including other groups left out of pulp adventure like non-whites (nicely attacked by the Mississippi Slim vignettes in the book) or the problems of a gay male couple in period.</div> </div> </div> </div>While diversity and representation is always high on our list of priorities, I'm not sure if Mississippi Slim counts, per se: many of the sample characters had their origin in playtests. Adventure!'s credits page makes note of a character named Marshall &quot;Slim&quot; Shady, who is doubtless supposed to be Mississippi Slim. Given the clear parallels to Marshall Mathers, aka Slim Shady, aka Eminem, I'm pretty sure Slim was intended to be a riff on Eminem. As Slim is referenced earlier as a blues musician, I'd guess the intent was to play against type in the same way that Eminem does as a prominent Caucasian rapper (a genre mostly filled with black artists), except in this case a Caucasian blues musician (again, a genre mostly filled with black artists). A neat idea for a character, certainly, but not one I'd personally hold up as an example of diverse characters.<br /> <br /> Yes, I may have thought about this too much, and it's entirely likely I'm wrong about the original intent of Slim. His ethnicity is never mentioned in the book, IIRC, so it could easily go either way. In any case, we're striving to do better with the new edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T05:47:30-08:00","id":1181974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/984849-supplements-to-adventure?p=1181881#post1181881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was supposed to be a book on that very subject for a different game line (about 10 years ago IIRC), looking at everything from women, blacks and gays to even German and Japanese nationals in the 20s and 30s, but I've no idea if it ever actually came out or even which game line it was meant for.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I believe Bruce Baugh was going to write that, and I'm sure that was for a FATE game which, interestingly, was written as an admitted love letter to Adventure! It never got published for reasons related to, I think, Mr. Baugh's health issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T12:34:24-08:00","id":1182044,"title":"","content":"That's a shame. I would've snapped it up in a heartbeat and used it as info and inspiration not just for Adventure! but for Mage, Changeling, Werewolf, Scion, Mutants &amp; Masterminds, Call of Cthulhu and other things as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T11:50:46-08:00","id":1182338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon